def ord_add(a, b):
    if not b:
        return list(a)
    k = len(b) - 1
    lead = b[k] + (a[k] if k < len(a) else 0)
    return list(b[:k]) + [lead] + list(a[k + 1:])
```

Why: write $a = (\text{terms of power} > k) + \omega^k a_k + (\text{lower terms})$. The lower terms of $a$ are smaller than $\omega^k$, and anything smaller than $\omega^k$ followed by $\omega^k$ is absorbed (just as $3 + \omega = \omega$). So $a + b = (\text{terms of } a \text{ of power} > k) + \omega^k (a_k + b_k) + (\text{lower terms of } b)$.
